Howard <hposner1@swarthmore.edu> wrote:
>   Just how often can one safely pray for help when in distress?
> Also, unrelated query, how do I get my pet to stay close? It seems to
> wander off quite a bit.

Well... if you're less than level 17, then your next prayer is 
guaranteed to be heard after 3498 turns, or 3298 if you have major 
trouble.  It might take up to 6996 at level 30.  And a whole lot 
more after you've been crowned, and even more if you've killed the 
wizard or performed the invocation.

But you probably don't have to worry about that.  In fact, even the 3298
number is longer than you usually need to wait.  Here's a table, which
given the TURNS since your last prayer, shows the CHANCE of being heard
if you have major trouble:

TURNS CHANCE of prayer success if you have major trouble
   0   22%
 150   50%
 300   66%
 500   88%
 650   90%
1000   95%
1550   99%

In any case, try to keep prayer a last resort.

Getting your pet to stay close can be hard.  I think that having some
tripe in your pocket helps, so I try to do that, but I don't know how
much it helps.  A leash or magic whistle is great, of course.  I usually 
don't bother with tin whistles but some people do.  Other than that, 
patience is the only way.

